  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks, Victor, you're verified. I checked order Q-7801 from Taqueria Luz. It was promised for 6:15 PM and handed to you at 6:45 PM, so it was 30 minutes late.\n\nAn earlier support contact tonight already dealt with this. A $2.99 account credit, equal to your delivery fee, was added to your account at 7:07 PM. That's the full compensation for a delivery that was 16\u201344 minutes late. I can't add anything more for the same problem, and late orders get account credit only, not a refund to your card.\n\nIs there anything else I can help with, such as a missing or wrong item on this order?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, I did get a credit from someone earlier, I think it was around 7pm. It was really late though, and that's a long time to wait for tacos. Is there anything else you can do?"
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I understand, Victor. Waiting that long for dinner is frustrating, and I'm sorry. The $2.99 credit is the most I can offer for a delivery that was 30 minutes late. The policy doesn't allow any extra compensation or goodwill credit on top of it, so I can't add more.\n\nIf something was wrong with the order itself, like a missing or incorrect item, tell me and I'll look into it. If you'd like to talk to a person about this, I can pass your case to a human specialist."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, I get it. The credit is what I've got, and I'd rather not wait around on a specialist for it. Nothing was missing or wrong with the food, so I'll leave it there. Thanks for checking."
  },
  {
